ve retail consumers. T2's mechanism, where consumers 'accept lower prices' because items are essential and prefer them at higher willingness to pay, is incoherent."},{"kind":"other","event_ids":["A12","A14","A16"],"reason":"Sources that the packet classes as verified_observation (Nilfisk) are mislabelled as company_assertion."},{"kind":"other","event_ids":["A9","A10"],"reason":"The rival theories share an identical retail-sales prediction, so it cannot discriminate between them."}],"suitable_for_training":false,"screen_reason":"Rejected. The episode is incomplete, with no recommendation or test stage (A18). It also contains material unsupported inference in both theories (A9, A10), misclassifies source types (A12, A14, A16), and gives near-duplicate theories with a non-discriminating shared prediction."}
